File: ends-because-misplaced.l4
  Hidden: no
  Range: 28:22-28:65
  Source: check
  Severity: DiagnosticSeverity_Error
  Code: check/ends-because-on-non-definition
  Message:
    @ends-because goes on a definition, a rule written with MEANS or DECIDE, whose author vouches that the rule's uses of itself come to an end.
    Here it is on `x`, an input, which is not a definition. A mark speaks for a whole definition, not for one of its inputs: to speak for the definition that reads this input, put the mark on a line of its own above that definition's GIVEN; otherwise remove it.

File: ends-because-misplaced.l4
  Hidden: no
  Range: 32:1-32:14
  Source: check
  Severity: DiagnosticSeverity_Error
  Code: check/ends-because-needs-reason
  Message:
    @ends-because needs a reason after it, on the same line. Here it has none, above `no reason given`.
    The reason is what a reader checks: a mark that says the calls end without saying why gives the reader nothing to check, so it is not accepted.
    Write the reason after the mark, for example: @ends-because each step moves one day nearer the end date, and the end date is fixed

